  "hypothesis": "The two single-knob winners compose: bounded MAP + polish (988356) and the prior-unit eigenvalue floor (988824) together give no wrong-mode posterior, first-pass fails <= 2/32, and cost between the two arms (+14% and -9% of 986080).",
  "reason": "Matched reference for every later arm at the new initialization defaults; the two fixes were only ever measured one at a time.",
  "conclusion": "Composes as expected. 32/32, 2 first-pass fails (g15_r90 rhat 1.20 / ess 9, g12_r0 rhat 1.05 / ess 66; the w200 set was g15_r90 + g5_r90), 0 final. g5_r90 recovers the truth basin (theta 1.33 vs 1.14, v0 -8.6 vs +15; the reference sat at theta 4.50 / v0 -104 on all chains). Posteriors agree with 986080 (median 0.03-0.07 sigma, widths 1.00-1.01) except g5_r90; identical to 988356 (max 0.21 sigma). Cost: sum wall +9.4% and sum steps +8.7% vs 986080, but 0.98 / 1.00 with the two truth-cosi-0.054 fits removed: g2_r0 234k and g2_r90 141k steps vs 98k / 61k in the reference, MAP on the cosi 0.05 wall with projected gradient 9.1 / 0.95 and one floored eigenvalue each. Preconditioner wall 42 s median (was 22). g8_r90 sampled the truth rotation mode (flip margin 0.14 nats; 986080 sampled theta + pi with the same shear). Face-on (truth cosi > 0.7, 8 fits): cosi pull median -0.38 sigma, min -1.04, mean offset -0.047, unchanged from the reference.",
